; {$scopedenums on}: a value of a scoped enumeration is not in scope (not
; even in its class's methods), a value it does not have, a value repeated
; in it, and a toggle that is neither on nor off.
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/scopedenums/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:4:25: error: redefinition of 'Red'
; CHECK: errors.pas:4:13: note: previous definition is here
; CHECK: errors.pas:15:13: error: use of undeclared identifier 'One'
; CHECK: errors.pas:18:8: error: use of undeclared identifier 'Green'
; CHECK: errors.pas:19:15: error: no value named 'Nope' in enumeration 'TColor'
; CHECK-NOT: error:

; RUN: not %pcc --mode=tp -c %S/Inputs/scopedenums/toggle.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=TOGGLE %s
; TOGGLE: toggle.pas:2:1: error: expected {$scopedenums on} or {$scopedenums off}

; objfpc: a qualified default parameter value, a type helper's members next
; to the values (TColor.Blue.Code, TColor.Count), a scoped enumeration in a
; class (TOuter.TKind.One); output as Free Pascal's.
; RUN: %pcc --mode=objfpc %S/Inputs/scopedenums/objfpc.pas -o %t.objfpc
; RUN: %t.objfpc | FileCheck --check-prefix=OBJFPC %s
; OBJFPC:      1 2
; OBJFPC-NEXT: 20 3
; OBJFPC-NEXT: 1 0
